;; Configuration for the documentation site, read by the docs-engine
;; (https://github.com/jlt-commons/docs-engine).
;;
;; Build it locally with `jolt site:build`/`jolt site:serve` (or, without
;; jolt, `bb site:build`/`bb site:serve` -- see .github/workflows/site.yml).
;; CI builds it on every push and pull request, and publishes from main:
;; the PUBLISH_SITE repository variable is "true" and GitHub Pages is
;; enabled.
{;; :base-path is what makes this a project site rather than an org one.
 ;; The site is served at https://b12n-oss.github.io/lambda-mvp-jnk/, so
 ;; every URL the engine emits needs that prefix. Leave it out and the
 ;; pages still render, but each one loads the ORGANIZATION site's
 ;; stylesheet and every asset 404s. The workflow has a check for exactly
 ;; this (same pattern as the lambda-mvp-jlt sibling's own site.yml).
 :base-path   "/lambda-mvp-jnk"

 :title       "lambda-mvp-jnk"
 :description "A shareable AWS Lambda custom runtime in jank (native Clojure compiled to native code via C++/Clang/LLVM), deployed as a container image, with a bb bench tool for reproducing a cold-vs-warm boot-time comparison against your own AWS account."}
